(function(E){ const x = E["exam-05"] = E["exam-05"] || {units:{}}; (x.units = x.units || {})["x05-r1"] = {"id":"x05-r1","patterns":["RA-nature","GT1-reviews","GT1-notices","PARA-cause","PARA-rules"],"title":{"en":"Reading 1: Passage 1 / Section 1","tr":"Reading 1: Passage 1 / Section 1","fa":"Reading ۱: متن ۱ (Passage 1) / بخش ۱ (Section 1)"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to decide TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN by checking hedges and missing details, and to complete notes with one word or a number copied from the passage.","tr":"Bu derste çekinceleri ve eksik ayrıntıları kontrol ederek TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN’a karar vermeyi ve notları metinden kopyalanan bir kelime ya da bir sayıyla tamamlamayı öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری با بررسی قیدهای احتیاط و جزئیاتِ جاافتاده بین TRUE، FALSE و NOT GIVEN تصمیم بگیری و یادداشت‌ها را با یک کلمه یا یک عدد که از متن کپی می‌کنی کامل کنی."},"objectiveGT":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to match needs to six short reviews, and to decide TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN about rules and advice in an information text.","tr":"Bu derste ihtiyaçları altı kısa yorumla eşleştirmeyi ve bir bilgi metnindeki kurallar ve tavsiyeler hakkında TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN’a karar vermeyi öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری نیازها را با شش نظر کوتاه جور کنی و درباره‌ی قانون‌ها و توصیه‌های یک متن اطلاع‌رسانی بین TRUE، FALSE و NOT GIVEN تصمیم بگیری."},"sessions":[["explain"],["drill"],["exit"]],"explain":{"title":{"en":"Reading Passage 1: a natural history","tr":"Reading Passage 1: bir doğa tarihi","fa":"Reading Passage 1: یک روایت از طبیعت"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to decide TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN by checking hedges and missing details, and to complete notes with one word or a number copied from the passage.","tr":"Bu derste çekinceleri ve eksik ayrıntıları kontrol ederek TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN’a karar vermeyi ve notları metinden kopyalanan bir kelime ya da bir sayıyla tamamlamayı öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری با بررسی قیدهای احتیاط و جزئیاتِ جاافتاده بین TRUE، FALSE و NOT GIVEN تصمیم بگیری و یادداشت‌ها را با یک کلمه یا یک عدد که از متن کپی می‌کنی کامل کنی."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"13"},{"label":{"en":"Time","tr":"Süre","fa":"زمان"},"value":{"en":"20 min","tr":"20 dk","fa":"۲۰ دقیقه"}},{"label":{"en":"Words","tr":"Kelime","fa":"کلمه"},"value":"~770"}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: an island lizard","tr":"Bu sınav: bir ada kertenkelesi","fa":"این آزمون: یک مارمولک جزیره‌ای"},"intro":{"en":"Animals, plants and ecosystems are the most common subject of Academic passages. Passage 1 tells the story in time order, so the questions also follow the passage from start to finish. Learn the cause-and-change words on the card first.","tr":"Hayvanlar, bitkiler ve ekosistemler Academic metinlerinin en sık konusudur. Passage 1 hikâyeyi zaman sırasıyla anlatır, bu yüzden sorular da metni baştan sona izler. Önce karttaki neden ve değişim kelimelerini öğren.","fa":"جانوران، گیاهان و زیست‌بوم‌ها رایج‌ترین موضوع متن‌های Academic هستند. Passage 1 داستان را به ترتیب زمان می‌گوید، پس سؤال‌ها هم متن را از اول تا آخر دنبال می‌کنند. اول کلمه‌های علت و تغییرِ روی کارت را یاد بگیر."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x05-r1-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["RA-nature","PARA-cause"],"often":{"pattern":"RA-nature","n":37,"of":120,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 37 of the last 120 passages","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 120 metnin 37’sinde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۳۷ متن از ۱۲۰ متنِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"An animal that nearly disappeared","tr":"Neredeyse yok olan bir hayvan","fa":"جانوری که نزدیک بود نابود شود"},"asks":{"en":"A natural history in time order: the animal and its home, what caused its decline, how it was found again, and the recovery programme step by step. Passage 1 is often this kind of account, with TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN and notes.","tr":"Zaman sırasına göre bir doğa tarihi: hayvan ve yaşadığı yer, azalmasına neyin yol açtığı, nasıl yeniden bulunduğu ve adım adım kurtarma programı. Passage 1 çoğu zaman bu türden bir anlatımdır; TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN ve notlarla gelir.","fa":"یک روایت از طبیعت به ترتیب زمان: جانور و زیستگاهش، چه چیزی باعث کم شدنش شد، چطور دوباره پیدا شد و برنامه‌ی نجاتش قدم به قدم. Passage 1 اغلب همین نوع روایت است، با TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN و یادداشت."},"fields":["The animal and its island","Causes of the decline","Rediscovery","Recovery plan","Breeding centre","Release","Today"],"words":[{"a":"declined","b":"numbers fell / became rare","tr":"azaldı","fa":"کم شد"},{"a":"on purpose","b":"deliberately / intended","tr":"kasıtlı olarak","fa":"عمداً"},{"a":"by accident","b":"nobody intended it / simply came ashore","tr":"kazara","fa":"تصادفی"},{"a":"extinct","b":"no longer exists / none left","tr":"nesli tükenmiş","fa":"منقرض"},{"a":"found again","b":"rediscovered","tr":"yeniden bulundu","fa":"دوباره پیدا شد"},{"a":"removed","b":"taken off / got rid of","tr":"uzaklaştırıldı","fa":"برداشته شد، بیرون برده شد"},{"a":"young","b":"babies / hatchlings","tr":"yavrular","fa":"بچه‌ها، نوزادها"},{"a":"released","b":"set free / let go into the wild","tr":"doğaya bırakıldı","fa":"رها شد"},{"a":"survived","b":"stayed alive / lasted","tr":"hayatta kaldı","fa":"زنده ماند"},{"a":"still debated","b":"not agreed / may never be settled","tr":"hâlâ tartışmalı","fa":"هنوز محل بحث"},{"a":"threat","b":"danger / risk","tr":"tehdit","fa":"تهدید"},{"a":"caused","b":"led to / were disastrous for","tr":"yol açtı","fa":"باعث شد"}],"traps":[{"en":"A hedge decides: \"Some scientists believe...\" does not mean scientists agree. A statement saying \"it is known\" or \"scientists agree\" is then FALSE.","tr":"Bir çekince karar verir: \"Bazı bilim insanları inanıyor...\" bilim insanlarının hemfikir olduğu anlamına gelmez. \"Biliniyor\" ya da \"bilim insanları hemfikir\" diyen ifade o zaman FALSE olur.","fa":"یک قید احتیاط تعیین‌کننده است: «بعضی دانشمندان معتقدند...» یعنی دانشمندان هم‌نظر نیستند. جمله‌ای که می‌گوید «معلوم است» یا «دانشمندان توافق دارند» در این حالت FALSE است."},{"en":"A detail the text does not give: the text says an expedition failed, but not how long it lasted. A statement about the length is NOT GIVEN, not FALSE.","tr":"Metnin vermediği bir ayrıntı: metin bir keşif gezisinin başarısız olduğunu söylüyor ama ne kadar sürdüğünü söylemiyor. Süre hakkındaki bir ifade FALSE değil NOT GIVEN’dır.","fa":"جزئیاتی که متن نمی‌دهد: متن می‌گوید یک سفر تحقیقاتی ناموفق بود، اما نمی‌گوید چقدر طول کشید. جمله‌ای درباره‌ی مدتش NOT GIVEN است، نه FALSE."},{"en":"Numbers in notes: copy the figure exactly as it is in the passage, with no extra words.","tr":"Notlardaki sayılar: rakamı metinde olduğu gibi, fazladan kelime olmadan kopyala.","fa":"عددها در یادداشت: عدد را دقیقاً همان‌طور که در متن آمده و بدون کلمه‌ی اضافه کپی کن."}],"example":{"text":"\"Cats reached the island in the 1890s, probably on a supply boat. Within twenty years the ground-nesting birds had almost gone.\"","item":"Statement: Cats were brought to the island to control the birds.","answer":"FALSE","why":{"en":"\"Probably on a supply boat\" = by accident, not to control the birds. The text gives a different reason, so FALSE.","tr":"\"Muhtemelen bir ikmal teknesiyle\" = kazara, kuşları kontrol için değil. Metin farklı bir neden veriyor, yani FALSE.","fa":"«احتمالاً با یک قایق تدارکات» یعنی تصادفی، نه برای کنترل پرنده‌ها. متن دلیل دیگری می‌دهد، پس FALSE."}}},{"id":"RA-nature-p1","ctx":["RA-nature"],"title":{"en":"Natural history accounts","tr":"Doğa tarihi anlatıları","fa":"روایت‌های تاریخ طبیعی"},"asks":{"en":"A factual account of an animal, a plant or a natural place: how it lives, how it was discovered, why it declined and how it is protected. Statements test single facts; the notes follow the order of the text.","tr":"Bir hayvan, bitki ya da doğal bir yer hakkında bilgilendirici bir metin: nasıl yaşadığı, nasıl keşfedildiği, neden azaldığı ve nasıl korunduğu. İfadeler tek tek bilgileri sınar; notlar metnin sırasını izler.","fa":"متنی اطلاعاتی درباره‌ی یک حیوان، یک گیاه یا یک مکان طبیعی: چطور زندگی می‌کند، چطور کشف شد، چرا کم شد و چطور از آن حفاظت می‌شود. جمله‌ها اطلاعات جزئی را می‌سنجند؛ یادداشت‌ها ترتیب متن را دنبال می‌کنند."},"fields":["The species was first described in the 1800s.","Its numbers have fallen since the 1950s.","It is found only on one island.","Farmers consider it a pest.","Notes: Diet · Habitat · Threats · Protection"],"words":[{"a":"declined","b":"fell in number / became scarcer","tr":"azaldı","fa":"کم شد"},{"a":"disappeared","b":"became extinct / died out","tr":"yok oldu","fa":"از بین رفت"},{"a":"only","b":"exclusively / nowhere else","tr":"yalnızca","fa":"فقط"},{"a":"first","b":"the earliest / originally","tr":"ilk","fa":"اولین"},{"a":"increased","b":"rose / grew / expanded","tr":"arttı","fa":"افزایش یافت"},{"a":"protect","b":"conserve / save from","tr":"korumak","fa":"حفاظت کردن"},{"a":"harmful","b":"damaging / a threat to","tr":"zararlı","fa":"مضر"},{"a":"common","b":"widespread / found in many places","tr":"yaygın","fa":"رایج"},{"a":"scientists","b":"researchers / biologists","tr":"bilim insanları","fa":"دانشمندان"},{"a":"uncertain","b":"it remains unclear / not yet known","tr":"belirsiz","fa":"نامعلوم"},{"a":"caused by","b":"the result of / due to","tr":"... yüzünden","fa":"ناشی از"},{"a":"brought in","b":"introduced by humans","tr":"dışarıdan getirilmiş","fa":"وارد شده"}],"traps":[{"en":"Hedging: \"may\", \"some researchers believe\". A statement that turns this into a fact is usually FALSE or NOT GIVEN; compare carefully.","tr":"Temkinli dil: \"may\", \"bazı araştırmacılara göre\". Bunu kesin bilgiye çeviren bir ifade genelde FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN olur; dikkatle karşılaştır.","fa":"زبان محتاطانه: «may»، «بعضی پژوهشگرها معتقدند». جمله‌ای که این را به واقعیت قطعی تبدیل کند معمولاً FALSE یا NOT GIVEN است؛ دقیق مقایسه کن."},{"en":"\"Only\", \"always\", \"never\" in a statement: one exception in the text makes it FALSE.","tr":"İfadede \"only\", \"always\", \"never\": metindeki tek bir istisna onu FALSE yapar.","fa":"«only»، «always»، «never» در جمله: یک استثنا در متن آن را FALSE می‌کند."},{"en":"Notes: two numbers or dates sit close together. The heading decides which one you need.","tr":"Notlar: iki sayı ya da tarih yan yanadır. Hangisinin gerektiğine başlık karar verir.","fa":"یادداشت‌ها: دو عدد یا تاریخ نزدیک هم‌اند. عنوان تعیین می‌کند کدام را لازم داری."}],"example":{"text":"The hazel dormouse was once found in woods across most of England. Its range has shrunk by about half since 1900, mainly because the hedges that linked woodlands were removed. Most surviving populations are now in the south.","item":"Statement: The dormouse has always lived only in the south of England.  (TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN)","answer":"FALSE","why":{"en":"\"Once found in woods across most of England\" contradicts \"always... only in the south\".","tr":"\"Bir zamanlar İngiltere’nin çoğunda\" bulunması, \"her zaman... yalnızca güneyde\" ile çelişiyor.","fa":"«زمانی در جنگل‌های بیشتر انگلستان بود» با «همیشه... فقط در جنوب» در تضاد است."}},"track":"academic","general":true,"patterns":["RA-nature"],"often":{"pattern":"RA-nature","n":37,"of":120,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 37 of the last 120 passages","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 120 metnin 37’sinde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۳۷ متن از ۱۲۰ متنِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Statements first, then notes","tr":"Önce ifadeler, sonra notlar","fa":"اول جمله‌ها، بعد یادداشت‌ها"},"body":{"en":"Questions 1-6: TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN, on the first half of the passage. Questions 7-13: notes on the second half, with ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage. Spend about 20 minutes; there is no extra time to copy answers.","tr":"Soru 1-6: metnin ilk yarısı üzerine TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN. Soru 7-13: ikinci yarı üzerine, metinden ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER ile notlar. Yaklaşık 20 dakika ayır; cevapları aktarmak için ek süre yok.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۱ تا ۶: TRUE، FALSE یا NOT GIVEN درباره‌ی نیمه‌ی اول متن. سؤال‌های ۷ تا ۱۳: یادداشت درباره‌ی نیمه‌ی دوم، با ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER از متن. حدود ۲۰ دقیقه وقت بگذار؛ زمان اضافه برای انتقال جواب‌ها نیست."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Four steps","tr":"Dört adım","fa":"چهار قدم"},"steps":[{"en":"Underline the key words of the statement: names, dates and words like first, deliberately, agree.","tr":"İfadenin anahtar kelimelerinin altını çiz: isimler, tarihler ve first, deliberately, agree gibi kelimeler.","fa":"زیر کلمه‌های کلیدی جمله خط بکش: اسم‌ها، تاریخ‌ها و کلمه‌هایی مثل first، deliberately، agree."},{"en":"Find the one sentence it is about and compare every detail, including how sure the writer is.","tr":"İlgili olduğu tek cümleyi bul ve yazarın ne kadar emin olduğu da dahil her ayrıntıyı karşılaştır.","fa":"همان یک جمله‌ی مربوط را پیدا کن و همه‌ی جزئیات را مقایسه کن، از جمله اینکه نویسنده چقدر مطمئن است."},{"en":"For notes, use the heading to find the paragraph, then copy the word or figure exactly.","tr":"Notlar için başlığı kullanarak paragrafı bul, sonra kelimeyi ya da rakamı aynen kopyala.","fa":"برای یادداشت‌ها با کمک عنوان پاراگراف را پیدا کن و بعد کلمه یا عدد را دقیقاً کپی کن."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"FALSE or NOT GIVEN?","tr":"FALSE mı NOT GIVEN mı?","fa":"FALSE یا NOT GIVEN؟"},"table":{"headers":{"en":["The text","The answer"],"tr":["Metin","Cevap"],"fa":["متن","جواب"]},"rows":[["says the same thing in other words","TRUE"],["says the opposite, or a different fact on the same point","FALSE"],["says nothing about this point","NOT GIVEN"]]}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One statement, step by step","tr":"Bir ifade, adım adım","fa":"یک جمله، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Do the following statements agree with the information given in the passage?","text":"\"Some researchers think the frogs disappeared because of a fungus. Others point to the dry summers of the 1990s.\"","item":"Statement: Researchers agree that a fungus killed the frogs.","answer":"FALSE","walk":[{"en":"Find the place: the sentence about why the frogs disappeared.","tr":"Yeri bul: kurbağaların neden yok olduğunu anlatan cümle.","fa":"جایش را پیدا کن: جمله‌ای که می‌گوید چرا قورباغه‌ها ناپدید شدند."},{"en":"Compare: \"some... others\" = two different views, so they do not agree.","tr":"Karşılaştır: \"bazıları... diğerleri\" = iki farklı görüş, yani hemfikir değiller.","fa":"مقایسه کن: «بعضی... بقیه» یعنی دو نظر متفاوت، پس توافق ندارند."},{"en":"The text contradicts \"agree\": FALSE, not NOT GIVEN.","tr":"Metin \"agree\" ile çelişiyor: NOT GIVEN değil, FALSE.","fa":"متن با «agree» تناقض دارد: FALSE، نه NOT GIVEN."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"Text: \"The first survey counted 80 nests.\" Statement: \"The first survey took place in spring.\" TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN?","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"The text gives the number of nests, but not the season of the survey.","tr":"Metin yuva sayısını veriyor ama araştırmanın mevsimini vermiyor.","fa":"متن تعداد لانه‌ها را می‌گوید، اما فصل بررسی را نمی‌گوید."}},"remember":{"en":"Check how sure the text is: \"some believe\" is not \"it is known\". A missing detail is NOT GIVEN.","tr":"Metnin ne kadar emin olduğuna bak: \"bazıları inanıyor\", \"biliniyor\" demek değildir. Eksik bir ayrıntı NOT GIVEN’dır.","fa":"ببین متن چقدر مطمئن است: «بعضی معتقدند» یعنی «معلوم است» نیست. جزئیاتی که نیامده NOT GIVEN است."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x05-r1-e","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-05","unit":"x05-r1"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"reading","part":"Academic Reading Passage 1","title":{"en":"The return of the Ravensey skink","tr":"Ravensey kertenkelesinin dönüşü","fa":"بازگشت سوسمار رِیوِنزی"},"timed":20,"ctx":["RA-nature"],"intro":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.","passage":"The return of the Ravensey skink\n\nRavensey is a small volcanic island, about twelve kilometres long, lying far out in the North Atlantic. Its high central ridge catches most of the rain, and its lower slopes were once covered in dense, low shrubs. For thousands of years its only land animals of any size were seabirds and reptiles. The largest of these reptiles, the Ravensey skink, can grow to forty-five centimetres and live for more than twenty years. It feeds mainly on fallen fruit and seeds, adding insects to its diet in summer, and as it moves around the island it spreads the seeds of several native shrubs. Without it, botanists believe, the island's plant life would look very different.\n\nEuropean ships first began to stop at Ravensey in the seventeenth century. Sailors left goats behind on purpose, so that later crews would find fresh meat waiting for them. Rats arrived at the same time, though nobody intended it: they simply came ashore from the ships. Both newcomers were disastrous for the skink. The goats stripped the hillsides of the shrubs that provided its food and shelter, while the rats ate its eggs and its young.\n\nThe decline was rapid. Visitors in the eighteenth century described skinks as common in every valley, but by 1900 naturalists who explored the island reported seeing only a handful. In 1931 a museum expedition searched the island and failed to find a single one, and in 1950 the species was officially declared extinct. For almost forty years it was known only from a few specimens kept in museum drawers.\n\nThen, in 1987, a bird researcher who was counting shearwater nests on the northern cliffs looked down and noticed a large lizard lying in the sun on a narrow ledge. She was not looking for reptiles at all, but she took photographs, and experts quickly confirmed that the animal was a Ravensey skink. A survey the following year found about 160 adults, all of them living on a strip of steep cliff where neither goats nor rats could reach them.\n\nWhy this small group had survived is still debated. Some scientists believe that the dark rock of the cliffs, which warms quickly in the sun, allowed the skinks' eggs to develop faster and so spend less time at risk. Others argue that the population survived largely by chance, and that the cliffs were simply the last place the rats had not yet reached. With so few records from the years in between, the question may never be settled.\n\nWhat was clear was that the cliff population could not grow on its own, and a recovery plan began in 1990. The first task was to remove the animals that had caused the decline. The last goats were taken off the island in 1994. The rats were harder to deal with, but after poison bait had been dropped from helicopters over two winters, the island was declared free of rats in 1999.\n\nAt the same time, a breeding centre was set up in the island's only village. Eggs were collected from the cliffs and kept in incubators at a steady 28 degrees, a temperature that produced healthy young in the largest numbers. The young skinks were then raised at the centre for three years, until they were too large to be eaten by gulls, which take many young lizards in the wild.\n\nThe first forty skinks were released in 2002 into a fenced valley in the south-west of the island, where volunteers had spent several years replanting native shrubs. Each animal carried a tiny radio transmitter, so that the team could follow its movements and find out which parts of the valley it preferred. Almost all of them survived their first year, and within five years young skinks born in the wild were being found outside the fence.\n\nBy 2020 the population had reached about 2,300, spread across most of the island, and the species was moved from \"critically endangered\" to \"vulnerable\". The work is not over, however. Rats could easily return on visiting yachts, so every boat must now be inspected before anyone is allowed to land. And because every skink alive today is descended from those 160 cliff survivors, the species has little genetic variety, which could leave it exposed to a new disease. To reduce this risk, a small group of skinks is now kept at a zoo on the mainland as a reserve population. For the islanders themselves, the animal has become a source of pride: it appears on the village sign, and children from the island school help with the spring count every year.","groups":[{"instruction":"Questions 1-6. Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","qtype":"tfng","questions":[{"n":1,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"The Ravensey skink helps some plants to spread across the island.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"it spreads the seeds of several native shrubs","why":{"en":"\"It spreads the seeds of several native shrubs\" = it helps them spread.","tr":"\"Birkaç yerli çalının tohumlarını yayıyor\" = yayılmalarına yardım ediyor.","fa":"«بذر چند بوته‌ی بومی را پخش می‌کند» یعنی به پخش شدنشان کمک می‌کند."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":2,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Rats were brought to Ravensey on purpose.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"though nobody intended it","why":{"en":"The goats were left on purpose; the rats came \"though nobody intended it\".","tr":"Keçiler kasıtlı bırakıldı; sıçanlar ise \"kimse istemeden\" geldi.","fa":"بزها عمداً جا گذاشته شدند؛ موش‌ها «بی‌آنکه کسی بخواهد» آمدند."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":3,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"The 1931 expedition spent several months on the island.","correct":"NOT GIVEN","evidence":"In 1931 a museum expedition searched the island","why":{"en":"The text says the expedition searched and failed; it does not say how long it stayed.","tr":"Metin keşif ekibinin aradığını ve başaramadığını söylüyor; ne kadar kaldığını söylemiyor.","fa":"متن می‌گوید گروه جستجو کرد و موفق نشد؛ نمی‌گوید چقدر ماند."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":4,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"The skink was rediscovered by a scientist who was searching for it.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"She was not looking for reptiles at all","why":{"en":"She was counting shearwater nests and \"was not looking for reptiles at all\".","tr":"Yelkovan kuşu yuvalarını sayıyordu ve \"hiç de sürüngen aramıyordu\".","fa":"داشت لانه‌های پرنده‌ها را می‌شمرد و «اصلاً دنبال خزنده‌ها نبود»."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":5,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"The skinks that survived were living somewhere that goats and rats could not reach.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"where neither goats nor rats could reach them","why":{"en":"\"A strip of steep cliff where neither goats nor rats could reach them.\"","tr":"\"Ne keçilerin ne de sıçanların ulaşabildiği dik bir yamaç şeridi.\"","fa":"«باریکه‌ای از صخره‌ی شیب‌دار که نه بزها به آن می‌رسیدند نه موش‌ها»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":6,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"It is known that warm rock helped the cliff skinks to survive.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"Some scientists believe that the dark rock","why":{"en":"Only \"some scientists believe\" it; others disagree and the question \"may never be settled\". \"It is known\" contradicts this.","tr":"Buna yalnızca \"bazı bilim insanları inanıyor\"; diğerleri katılmıyor ve soru \"belki hiç çözülmeyecek\". \"Biliniyor\" bununla çelişiyor.","fa":"فقط «بعضی دانشمندان معتقدند»؛ بقیه مخالف‌اند و این سؤال «شاید هیچ‌وقت حل نشود». «معلوم است» با این تناقض دارد."},"trap":["TR-hedge","TR-NGvsF"]}]},{"instruction":"Questions 7-13. Complete the notes below. Choose ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 7-13 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"note","notesTitle":"Saving the Ravensey skink","questions":[{"n":7,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Recovery plan · the last goats were removed in ___","accept":["1994"],"limit":1,"evidence":"The last goats were taken off the island in 1994","why":{"en":"\"The last goats were taken off the island in 1994\": removed = taken off.","tr":"\"Son keçiler 1994’te adadan çıkarıldı\": removed = taken off.","fa":"«آخرین بزها در ۱۹۹۴ از جزیره برده شدند»: removed یعنی taken off."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":8,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Recovery plan · poison bait for rats was dropped from ___","accept":["helicopters"],"limit":1,"evidence":"poison bait had been dropped from helicopters","why":{"en":"\"Poison bait had been dropped from helicopters.\" Keep the plural.","tr":"\"Zehirli yem helikopterlerden atılmıştı.\" Çoğulu koru.","fa":"«طعمه‌ی سمی از هلی‌کوپترها ریخته شده بود». جمع را نگه دار."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":9,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Breeding centre · eggs kept in incubators at ___ degrees","accept":["28"],"limit":1,"evidence":"kept in incubators at a steady 28 degrees","why":{"en":"\"At a steady 28 degrees\". \"degrees\" is printed: write the number only.","tr":"\"Sabit 28 derecede\". \"degrees\" yazılı: yalnızca sayıyı yaz.","fa":"«در دمای ثابت ۲۸ درجه». «degrees» چاپ شده: فقط عدد را بنویس."},"trap":["TR-limit"]},{"n":10,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Breeding centre · young raised until too large to be eaten by ___","accept":["gulls"],"limit":1,"evidence":"too large to be eaten by gulls","why":{"en":"\"Until they were too large to be eaten by gulls.\"","tr":"\"Martıların yiyemeyeceği kadar büyüyene dek.\"","fa":"«تا وقتی آن‌قدر بزرگ شوند که مرغ‌های دریایی نتوانند بخورندشان»."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":11,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Release · first skinks released into a valley where native ___ had been replanted","accept":["shrubs"],"limit":1,"evidence":"replanting native shrubs","why":{"en":"\"Volunteers had spent several years replanting native shrubs.\"","tr":"\"Gönüllüler birkaç yıl yerli çalıları yeniden dikmişti.\"","fa":"«داوطلب‌ها چند سال بوته‌های بومی را دوباره کاشته بودند»."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":12,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Release · each skink carried a radio ___","accept":["transmitter"],"limit":1,"evidence":"Each animal carried a tiny radio transmitter","why":{"en":"\"Each animal carried a tiny radio transmitter\": one word, singular.","tr":"\"Her hayvan küçük bir radyo vericisi taşıyordu\": tek kelime, tekil.","fa":"«هر جانور یک فرستنده‌ی رادیویی کوچک داشت»: یک کلمه، مفرد."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":13,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Today · rats could come back on visiting ___","accept":["yachts"],"limit":1,"evidence":"Rats could easily return on visiting yachts","why":{"en":"\"Rats could easily return on visiting yachts\": come back = return.","tr":"\"Sıçanlar ziyarete gelen yatlarla kolayca geri dönebilir\": come back = return.","fa":"«موش‌ها به‌راحتی می‌توانند با قایق‌های تفریحیِ مهمان برگردند»: come back یعنی return."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase","TR-plural"]}]}],"id":"c-x05-r1-d","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-05","unit":"x05-r1"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"The species was officially declared extinct.\" This means...","options":["it was moved to a zoo","it was announced that none were left alive","it became protected by law"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"Extinct = no longer existing; declared = officially announced.","tr":"Extinct = artık var olmayan; declared = resmen açıklandı.","fa":"extinct یعنی دیگر وجود ندارد؛ declared یعنی رسماً اعلام شد."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":1,"prompt":"A statement says \"by accident\". Which words in a passage mean the same?","options":["though nobody intended it","on purpose","as planned"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"If nobody intended it, it happened by accident.","tr":"Kimse istemediyse kazara olmuştur.","fa":"اگر کسی قصدش را نداشته، تصادفی اتفاق افتاده."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"Notes say ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER. The passage says \"about 2,300 animals\". The note is \"population in 2020: about ___\". You write...","options":["2,300 animals","about 2,300","2,300"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"\"about\" is printed and \"animals\" is extra: write the number only.","tr":"\"about\" yazılı, \"animals\" fazladan: yalnızca sayıyı yaz.","fa":"«about» چاپ شده و «animals» اضافه است: فقط عدد را بنویس."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Text: \"Some experts think the birds left because of the noise.\" Statement: \"Experts agree that noise drove the birds away.\"","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"\"Some experts think\" is not agreement among experts, so the statement goes against the text.","tr":"\"Bazı uzmanlar düşünüyor\" uzmanların hemfikir olduğu anlamına gelmez; ifade metinle çelişiyor.","fa":"«بعضی کارشناس‌ها فکر می‌کنند» یعنی کارشناس‌ها توافق ندارند، پس جمله با متن تناقض دارد."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Text: \"A team searched the forest in 1960 and found nothing.\" Statement: \"The 1960 team searched for two weeks.\"","options":["NOT GIVEN","FALSE","TRUE"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"The year and the result are given; the length of the search is not.","tr":"Yıl ve sonuç veriliyor; aramanın süresi verilmiyor.","fa":"سال و نتیجه آمده؛ مدت جستجو نیامده."}}],"id":"c-x05-r1-x","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-05","unit":"x05-r1"},"gt":{"explain":{"title":{"en":"GT Reading Section 1: reviews and visitor information","tr":"GT Reading Section 1: yorumlar ve ziyaretçi bilgisi","fa":"GT Reading Section 1: نظرها و اطلاعات بازدیدکننده"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to match needs to six short reviews, and to decide TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN about rules and advice in an information text.","tr":"Bu derste ihtiyaçları altı kısa yorumla eşleştirmeyi ve bir bilgi metnindeki kurallar ve tavsiyeler hakkında TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN’a karar vermeyi öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری نیازها را با شش نظر کوتاه جور کنی و درباره‌ی قانون‌ها و توصیه‌های یک متن اطلاع‌رسانی بین TRUE، FALSE و NOT GIVEN تصمیم بگیری."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"14"},{"label":{"en":"Texts","tr":"Metin","fa":"متن"},"value":"2"},{"label":{"en":"Time","tr":"Süre","fa":"زمان"},"value":{"en":"about 15 min","tr":"yaklaşık 15 dk","fa":"حدود ۱۵ دقیقه"}}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: cottages and city walks","tr":"Bu sınav: tatil evleri ve şehir yürüyüşleri","fa":"این آزمون: کلبه‌ها و پیاده‌روی در شهر"},"intro":{"en":"GT Section 1 is everyday texts: reviews, adverts, notices. Short reviews with letters A-F are one of the most common first texts. Read the questions first, then scan each review for the meaning, not the same word.","tr":"GT Section 1 günlük metinlerdir: yorumlar, ilanlar, duyurular. A-F harfli kısa yorumlar en sık çıkan ilk metinlerdendir. Önce soruları oku, sonra her yorumu aynı kelimeyi değil anlamı arayarak tara.","fa":"GT Section 1 متن‌های روزمره است: نظرها، آگهی‌ها، اطلاعیه‌ها. نظرهای کوتاه با حرف‌های A تا F از رایج‌ترین متن‌های اول هستند. اول سؤال‌ها را بخوان، بعد هر نظر را دنبال معنی بگرد، نه همان کلمه."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x05-r1gt-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["GT1-reviews","GT1-notices","PARA-rules"],"often":{"pattern":"GT1-reviews","n":19,"of":65,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 19 of the last 65 texts","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 65 metnin 19’unda","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۹ متن از ۶۵ متنِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"Holiday cottage reviews and a walking guide","tr":"Tatil evi yorumları ve bir yürüyüş rehberi","fa":"نظرهای مهمان درباره‌ی کلبه‌ها و یک راهنمای پیاده‌روی"},"asks":{"en":"Text 1 is six short reviews, A-F: you decide which place matches each need. Text 2 is information for visitors, with rules and advice: you decide TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN.","tr":"Metin 1, A-F arası altı kısa yorumdur: her ihtiyaca hangi yerin uyduğuna karar verirsin. Metin 2, kurallar ve tavsiyeler içeren ziyaretçi bilgisidir: TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN’a karar verirsin.","fa":"متن ۱ شش نظر کوتاه است، A تا F: تصمیم می‌گیری کدام جا با هر نیاز جور است. متن ۲ اطلاعاتی برای بازدیدکننده‌هاست، با قانون و توصیه: بین TRUE، FALSE و NOT GIVEN تصمیم می‌گیری."},"fields":["Who it suits","What is not allowed","Noise and location","Pets","Minimum stay","Rules for walkers","Free services"],"words":[{"a":"suitable for wheelchair users","b":"step-free access / ground-floor bedroom","tr":"tekerlekli sandalye kullananlara uygun","fa":"مناسب برای کسی که ویلچر دارد"},{"a":"pets welcome","b":"dogs are allowed","tr":"evcil hayvan kabul edilir","fa":"حیوان خانگی مجاز است"},{"a":"not suitable for young children","b":"guests aged twelve and over only","tr":"küçük çocuklara uygun değil","fa":"برای بچه‌های کوچک مناسب نیست"},{"a":"noisy","b":"starts at five in the morning / be warned","tr":"gürültülü","fa":"پرسروصدا"},{"a":"minimum stay","b":"can only be booked for at least","tr":"en az kalış süresi","fa":"حداقل مدت اقامت"},{"a":"free","b":"at no cost / no charge","tr":"ücretsiz","fa":"رایگان"},{"a":"have priority","b":"have right of way","tr":"önceliği olmak","fa":"حق تقدم داشتن"},{"a":"not permitted","b":"not allowed / must not","tr":"izin verilmez","fa":"مجاز نیست"},{"a":"shared with","b":"used by both walkers and cyclists","tr":"... ile ortak kullanılır","fa":"مشترک با"},{"a":"no need to book","b":"just turn up","tr":"rezervasyon gerekmez","fa":"لازم نیست رزرو کنی"},{"a":"we recommend","b":"advice, not a law","tr":"öneriyoruz","fa":"توصیه می‌کنیم"},{"a":"optional","b":"entirely up to you","tr":"isteğe bağlı","fa":"اختیاری"}],"traps":[{"en":"Same words, wrong place: a review that mentions dogs may say they are not allowed inside. Match the meaning, not the word.","tr":"Aynı kelimeler, yanlış yer: köpeklerden söz eden bir yorum, içeri alınmadıklarını söylüyor olabilir. Kelimeyi değil anlamı eşleştir.","fa":"کلمه‌های یکسان، جای غلط: نظری که از سگ حرف می‌زند ممکن است بگوید داخل خانه مجاز نیستند. معنی را جور کن، نه کلمه را."},{"en":"Advice is not a law: \"We recommend not...\" does not make something illegal. A statement about the law is then NOT GIVEN.","tr":"Tavsiye kanun değildir: \"... yapmamanızı öneririz\" bir şeyi yasa dışı yapmaz. Kanunla ilgili bir ifade o zaman NOT GIVEN olur.","fa":"توصیه قانون نیست: «توصیه می‌کنیم... نکنید» چیزی را غیرقانونی نمی‌کند. جمله‌ای درباره‌ی قانون در این حالت NOT GIVEN است."}],"example":{"text":"\"The museum café is closed on Mondays. The museum itself is open every day.\"","item":"Statement: Visitors cannot enter the museum on Mondays.","answer":"FALSE","why":{"en":"Only the café closes; the museum is \"open every day\". The statement contradicts the text.","tr":"Yalnızca kafe kapalı; müze \"her gün açık\". İfade metinle çelişiyor.","fa":"فقط کافه بسته است؛ موزه «هر روز باز است». جمله با متن تناقض دارد."}}},{"id":"GT1-reviews","ctx":["GT1-reviews"],"title":{"en":"Product and service reviews","tr":"Ürün ve hizmet değerlendirmeleri","fa":"نقد و معرفی کالا و خدمات"},"asks":{"en":"Short reviews or descriptions A-F of products or places: sleeping bags, kitchen machines, cafes, hotels, phone apps. Questions ask which one has a feature, or which review says something.","tr":"Ürünler ya da yerler hakkında A-F harfli kısa değerlendirmeler veya tanıtımlar: uyku tulumları, mutfak aletleri, kafeler, oteller, telefon uygulamaları. Sorular hangisinin bir özelliği olduğunu ya da hangi yorumun bir şey söylediğini sorar.","fa":"نقدها یا معرفی‌های کوتاه A تا F درباره‌ی کالاها یا مکان‌ها: کیسه‌خواب، وسایل آشپزخانه، کافه، هتل، اپلیکیشن. سؤال‌ها می‌پرسند کدام یک ویژگی را دارد، یا کدام نقد چیزی را می‌گوید."},"fields":["Which sleeping bag is the lightest?","Which cafe has outdoor seating?","Which app works without the internet?","Which hotel is suitable for families?"],"words":[{"a":"lightweight","b":"weighs very little / easy to carry","tr":"hafif","fa":"سبک"},{"a":"durable","b":"lasts for years / hard-wearing","tr":"dayanıklı","fa":"بادوام"},{"a":"value for money","b":"a good price for what you get","tr":"fiyatına değer","fa":"به‌صرفه"},{"a":"noisy","b":"loud","tr":"gürültülü","fa":"پرسروصدا"},{"a":"spacious","b":"lots of room","tr":"ferah","fa":"جادار"},{"a":"easy to clean","b":"wipes clean","tr":"kolay temizlenir","fa":"راحت تمیز می‌شود"},{"a":"offline","b":"without an internet connection","tr":"çevrimdışı","fa":"آفلاین"},{"a":"outdoor seating","b":"tables outside","tr":"dışarıda oturma yeri","fa":"میز در فضای باز"},{"a":"guarantee","b":"free repairs for two years","tr":"garanti","fa":"گارانتی"},{"a":"compact","b":"small / takes up little space","tr":"küçük, kompakt","fa":"جمع‌وجور"},{"a":"fully booked","b":"no rooms left","tr":"tamamen dolu","fa":"کاملاً پر"},{"a":"suitable for families","b":"children welcome / cots available","tr":"ailelere uygun","fa":"مناسب خانواده"}],"traps":[{"en":"Superlatives: \"the lightest\" needs a comparison with all the others, not just the word \"light\".","tr":"Üstünlük sıfatları: \"en hafif\" diğerlerinin hepsiyle karşılaştırma ister, yalnızca \"hafif\" kelimesi yetmez.","fa":"صفت عالی: «سبک‌ترین» یعنی مقایسه با همه‌ی بقیه، نه فقط کلمه‌ی «سبک»."},{"en":"A review may mention a feature only to say that it is missing.","tr":"Bir yorum bir özellikten yalnızca eksik olduğunu söylemek için bahsedebilir.","fa":"یک نقد ممکن است به ویژگی‌ای فقط اشاره کند تا بگوید ندارد."}],"example":{"text":"A  The Trekker 200 weighs 900 g and packs down small.\nB  The Summit weighs just 650 g, though it is not quite as warm.\nC  The Polar Pro is the warmest of the three, at 1.4 kg.","item":"Which sleeping bag is the lightest?","answer":"B","why":{"en":"Compare all three: 650 g is less than 900 g and 1.4 kg.","tr":"Üçünü de karşılaştır: 650 g, 900 g ve 1,4 kg’dan az.","fa":"هر سه را مقایسه کن: ۶۵۰ گرم از ۹۰۰ گرم و ۱٫۴ کیلو کمتر است."}},"track":"gt","general":true,"patterns":["GT1-reviews"],"often":{"pattern":"GT1-reviews","n":19,"of":65,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 19 of the last 65 texts","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 65 metnin 19’unda","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۹ متن از ۶۵ متنِ اخیر"}}},{"id":"GT1-notices","ctx":["GT1-notices"],"title":{"en":"Notices, rules and FAQs","tr":"Duyurular, kurallar ve SSS","fa":"اطلاعیه، قانون و پرسش‌های متداول"},"asks":{"en":"Notices, rules and frequently asked questions for a service: a tram, a leisure centre, a block of flats, a competition. Questions test rules, conditions, dates and exceptions.","tr":"Bir hizmet için duyurular, kurallar ve sık sorulan sorular: tramvay, spor merkezi, apartman, yarışma. Sorular kuralları, koşulları, tarihleri ve istisnaları sınar.","fa":"اطلاعیه، قانون و پرسش‌های متداول برای یک خدمت: تراموا، مرکز ورزشی، یک ساختمان مسکونی، یک مسابقه. سؤال‌ها قانون‌ها، شرط‌ها، تاریخ‌ها و استثناها را می‌سنجند."},"fields":["Passengers must buy a ticket before boarding.","Children under five travel free.","Refunds are given for delays of over 30 minutes.","Residents may leave bicycles in the hallway."],"words":[{"a":"must","b":"are required to","tr":"zorunda","fa":"باید"},{"a":"not allowed","b":"prohibited / not permitted","tr":"yasak","fa":"ممنوع"},{"a":"within 14 days","b":"in less than two weeks","tr":"14 gün içinde","fa":"ظرف ۱۴ روز"},{"a":"can claim","b":"are entitled to / are eligible for","tr":"talep edebilir","fa":"می‌تواند درخواست کند"},{"a":"apply","b":"submit a form","tr":"başvurmak","fa":"درخواست دادن"},{"a":"proof","b":"a receipt / evidence of","tr":"kanıt","fa":"مدرک"},{"a":"residents","b":"people living in the building","tr":"sakinler","fa":"ساکنان"},{"a":"compensation","b":"money for a problem you had","tr":"tazminat","fa":"غرامت"},{"a":"beforehand","b":"in advance","tr":"önceden","fa":"از قبل"},{"a":"except","b":"apart from / with the exception of","tr":"hariç","fa":"به‌جز"},{"a":"responsible for","b":"must take care of","tr":"... -den sorumlu","fa":"مسئولِ"},{"a":"on request","b":"if you ask","tr":"talep üzerine","fa":"در صورت درخواست"}],"traps":[{"en":"Exceptions: \"all passengers must..., except season-ticket holders\". A statement about everyone may be FALSE.","tr":"İstisnalar: \"bütün yolcular ... zorunda, abonman sahipleri hariç\". Herkes hakkındaki bir ifade FALSE olabilir.","fa":"استثناها: «همه‌ی مسافران باید...، به‌جز دارندگان بلیت فصلی». جمله‌ای درباره‌ی همه ممکن است FALSE باشد."},{"en":"Numbers in conditions: \"30 minutes or more\" and \"over 30 minutes\" are not the same.","tr":"Koşullardaki sayılar: \"30 dakika veya daha fazla\" ile \"30 dakikadan fazla\" aynı değildir.","fa":"عددها در شرط‌ها: «۳۰ دقیقه یا بیشتر» با «بیش از ۳۰ دقیقه» یکی نیست."}],"example":{"text":"Delay Repay: if your train arrives 30 minutes or more late, you can claim 50% of your ticket price. Claims must be made within 28 days of travel.","item":"Statement: Passengers can claim the full price of their ticket.  (TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN)","answer":"FALSE","why":{"en":"The notice says 50%, which contradicts \"the full price\".","tr":"Duyuru %50 diyor; bu \"tam fiyat\" ile çelişiyor.","fa":"اطلاعیه می‌گوید ۵۰٪، که با «قیمت کامل» در تضاد است."}},"track":"gt","general":true,"patterns":["GT1-notices"],"often":{"pattern":"GT1-notices","n":22,"of":65,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 22 of the last 65 texts","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 65 metnin 22’sinde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۲۲ متن از ۶۵ متنِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Two texts, two tasks","tr":"İki metin, iki görev","fa":"دو متن، دو تمرین"},"body":{"en":"Questions 1-5: which review, A-F, matches each statement? A letter can be used more than once, and one or more letters are not used. Questions 6-14: TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN on the second text. Aim to finish Section 1 in about 15 minutes.","tr":"Soru 1-5: her ifadeye A-F’den hangi yorum uyuyor? Bir harf birden fazla kullanılabilir ve bir ya da daha fazla harf kullanılmaz. Soru 6-14: ikinci metin üzerine TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN. Section 1’i yaklaşık 15 dakikada bitirmeye çalış.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۱ تا ۵: کدام نظر، A تا F، با هر جمله جور است؟ یک حرف می‌تواند بیش از یک بار بیاید و یک یا چند حرف استفاده نمی‌شوند. سؤال‌های ۶ تا ۱۴: TRUE، FALSE یا NOT GIVEN درباره‌ی متن دوم. سعی کن Section 1 را در حدود ۱۵ دقیقه تمام کنی."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Need first, then scan","tr":"Önce ihtiyaç, sonra tarama","fa":"اول نیاز، بعد مرور سریع"},"steps":[{"en":"Turn each question into one need: wheelchair, children, noise, pets, length of stay.","tr":"Her soruyu tek bir ihtiyaca çevir: tekerlekli sandalye, çocuk, gürültü, evcil hayvan, kalış süresi.","fa":"هر سؤال را به یک نیاز تبدیل کن: ویلچر، بچه، سروصدا، حیوان خانگی، مدت اقامت."},{"en":"Scan all six reviews for that meaning, then read the sentence closely before you choose.","tr":"Altı yorumun hepsinde bu anlamı tara, seçmeden önce cümleyi dikkatle oku.","fa":"هر شش نظر را برای همین معنی مرور کن و قبل از انتخاب، جمله را با دقت بخوان."},{"en":"For TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN, check whether the text gives a rule, a piece of advice, or nothing.","tr":"TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN için metnin bir kural mı, bir tavsiye mi verdiğine yoksa hiçbir şey mi söylemediğine bak.","fa":"برای TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN ببین متن یک قانون می‌دهد، یک توصیه یا هیچ."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"The word is there, the meaning is not","tr":"Kelime orada, anlam yok","fa":"کلمه هست، معنی نیست"},"body":{"en":"Two reviews may use the same key word. One says dogs are welcome; another mentions dog walks but says pets are not allowed inside. Read the whole sentence: the answer is the review whose meaning matches the question.","tr":"İki yorum aynı anahtar kelimeyi kullanabilir. Biri köpeklerin kabul edildiğini söyler; diğeri köpek yürüyüşlerinden söz eder ama evcil hayvanların içeri alınmadığını söyler. Cümlenin tamamını oku: cevap, anlamı soruya uyan yorumdur.","fa":"ممکن است دو نظر همان کلمه‌ی کلیدی را داشته باشند. یکی می‌گوید سگ‌ها مجازند؛ دیگری از پیاده‌روی با سگ حرف می‌زند ولی می‌گوید حیوان خانگی داخل خانه مجاز نیست. کل جمله را بخوان: جواب نظری است که معنی‌اش با سؤال جور است."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One review, step by step","tr":"Bir yorum, adım adım","fa":"یک نظر، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Which hotel would suit someone who needs to work during their stay?","text":"\"A  Lovely pool, but the wifi only works in the lobby.\" · \"B  Every room has a large desk and fast internet, and there is a quiet business lounge.\"","item":"Which hotel, A or B?","answer":"B","walk":[{"en":"Need: a place to work, so a desk and good internet.","tr":"İhtiyaç: çalışacak bir yer, yani bir masa ve iyi internet.","fa":"نیاز: جایی برای کار، یعنی میز و اینترنت خوب."},{"en":"A mentions wifi, but \"only works in the lobby\" is a problem, not a help.","tr":"A wifi’den söz ediyor ama \"yalnızca lobide çalışıyor\" bir sorun, yardım değil.","fa":"A از وای‌فای حرف می‌زند، اما «فقط در لابی کار می‌کند» مشکل است، نه کمک."},{"en":"B: desk, fast internet and a quiet lounge match the need.","tr":"B: masa, hızlı internet ve sessiz salon ihtiyaca uyuyor.","fa":"B: میز، اینترنت سریع و سالن آرام با نیاز جور است."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"Text: \"Children under five travel free.\" Statement: \"Children under five do not need a ticket.\" TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN?","options":["NOT GIVEN","TRUE","FALSE"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Free travel does not tell you whether a (free) ticket is still needed. The text says nothing about tickets.","tr":"Ücretsiz yolculuk, (ücretsiz) bir biletin yine de gerekip gerekmediğini söylemez. Metin bilet hakkında bir şey söylemiyor.","fa":"رایگان بودن سفر نمی‌گوید آیا هنوز بلیت (رایگان) لازم است یا نه. متن درباره‌ی بلیت چیزی نمی‌گوید."}},"remember":{"en":"Match the meaning, not the word; and a rule, a piece of advice and silence are three different answers.","tr":"Kelimeyi değil anlamı eşleştir; kural, tavsiye ve sessizlik üç farklı cevaptır.","fa":"معنی را جور کن، نه کلمه را؛ قانون، توصیه و سکوتِ متن سه جواب متفاوت‌اند."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x05-r1-e-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-05","unit":"x05-r1"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"reading","part":"General Training Reading Section 1","title":{"en":"Holiday cottages and walking in the city","tr":"Tatil evleri ve şehirde yürüyüş","fa":"کلبه‌های تعطیلات و پیاده‌روی در شهر"},"timed":20,"ctx":["GT1-reviews","GT1-notices"],"texts":[{"title":"Holiday cottages on the Tregarra coast: guest reviews","kind":"reviews","body":"A  Gorse Cottage\nA traditional stone cottage with a wood-burning stove and a lovely sheltered garden. It is a fifteen-minute walk down a steep lane to the village, and back up again, so you really need a car. There are wonderful dog walks along the cliffs nearby, but sadly the owners do not allow pets inside.\n\nB  The Old Dairy\nPerfect for our family of eight. The games room kept the teenagers busy on a rainy day. My father uses a wheelchair, and there is a bedroom and bathroom on the ground floor with step-free access from the parking space, which made all the difference.\n\nC  Lookout Cottage\nThe view from the sitting room is breathtaking: you can see the whole bay. Because the garden ends at an unfenced cliff edge, the owners only accept guests aged twelve and over, which we understood. Ideal for couples. The beds were comfortable, and the owners had left a cake and a list of their favourite local walks.\n\nD  Millrace\nA converted mill beside a fast stream. The garden is completely fenced, and up to two dogs are welcome, with towels and bowls provided. Our spaniel had the holiday of his life. The kitchen is small but well equipped, and the village shop is only five minutes away on foot.\n\nE  Fisherman's Rest\nRight in the middle of the village, so you can walk to the restaurants and the harbour, which our children loved. Be warned: the cottage is above a bakery, and the ovens start at five in the morning. The smell of fresh bread almost makes up for it.\n\nF  Willow Barn\nA modern barn with solar panels and a charger for electric cars. Everything is beautifully designed. In July and August the barn can only be booked for a minimum of seven nights, so we came in June for a long weekend instead."},{"title":"Walking in Halbrook: information for visitors","kind":"article","body":"Halbrook's compact centre is best explored on foot, and most of the main sights are within twenty minutes' walk of each other. Walking is also the cheapest way to see the city, and it lets you discover the small courtyards and lanes that buses and taxis cannot reach. This guide explains what visitors need to know.\n\nStreets and paths\nIn the old town, where many streets are too narrow for pavements, pedestrians always have right of way, and vehicles must travel at walking pace. Outside the old town, please use the marked crossings: drivers in Halbrook are not used to people stepping into the road elsewhere. The riverside path is one of the most pleasant routes in the city, but it is shared with cyclists, so please keep to the left-hand side and listen out for bells.\n\nGuided walks\nFree walking tours leave from the steps of the Corn Exchange every Saturday and Sunday at 10.30 am. There is no need to book: simply turn up a few minutes early. The guides are local volunteers, and each tour lasts about ninety minutes. Many walkers choose to leave a small donation at the end, but this is entirely up to you.\n\nMaps and the city app\nFree paper maps are available from the information desk at the central railway station and from most hotels. Alternatively, the Halbrook Walks app, which can be downloaded at no cost, shows step-free routes for people with pushchairs or wheelchairs, as well as the nearest pharmacy at any point on your walk.\n\nAfter dark\nHalbrook is generally a safe city to walk around at night. The main streets are well lit until 1 am, after which every second street lamp is switched off to save energy. Victoria Park remains open all night, though some visitors may prefer to keep to its main avenue, which is lit, rather than the smaller paths.\n\nStaying safe\nWe recommend that walkers do not wear headphones when crossing busy roads, and that they carry a small bottle of water in summer, when temperatures in the centre can be several degrees higher than on the hills around the city. In an emergency, call 999."}],"groups":[{"text":0,"instruction":"Questions 1-5. Look at the six reviews, A-F, of holiday cottages. For which cottage are the following statements true? Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once.","qtype":"match-info","bank":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"questions":[{"n":1,"kind":"match","prompt":"This cottage would suit a guest who uses a wheelchair.","correct":1,"evidence":"step-free access from the parking space","why":{"en":"B: \"a bedroom and bathroom on the ground floor with step-free access\".","tr":"B: \"zemin katta basamaksız girişli bir yatak odası ve banyo\".","fa":"B: «یک اتاق خواب و حمام در طبقه‌ی همکف با ورودی بدون پله»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":2,"kind":"match","prompt":"Young children are not allowed to stay here.","correct":2,"evidence":"the owners only accept guests aged twelve and over","why":{"en":"C: guests \"aged twelve and over\" only, because of the cliff edge.","tr":"C: uçurum kenarı yüzünden yalnızca \"on iki yaş ve üstü\" misafirler.","fa":"C: فقط مهمان‌های «دوازده سال به بالا»، به‌خاطر لبه‌ی صخره."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":3,"kind":"match","prompt":"Guests may be disturbed early in the morning.","correct":4,"evidence":"the ovens start at five in the morning","why":{"en":"E: it is above a bakery and \"the ovens start at five in the morning\". The children in E are a distractor.","tr":"E: bir fırının üstünde ve \"fırınlar sabah beşte çalışmaya başlıyor\". E’deki çocuklar çeldirici.","fa":"E: بالای یک نانوایی است و «تنورها ساعت پنج صبح روشن می‌شوند». بچه‌ها در E گزینه‌ی انحرافی‌اند."},"trap":["TR-detail"]},{"n":4,"kind":"match","prompt":"This is a good choice for guests who want to bring a dog.","correct":3,"evidence":"up to two dogs are welcome","why":{"en":"D: \"up to two dogs are welcome\". A mentions dog walks, but pets are not allowed inside.","tr":"D: \"iki köpeğe kadar kabul ediliyor\". A köpek yürüyüşlerinden söz ediyor ama evcil hayvanlar içeri alınmıyor.","fa":"D: «تا دو سگ پذیرفته می‌شوند». A از پیاده‌روی با سگ حرف می‌زند، ولی حیوان خانگی داخل مجاز نیست."},"trap":["TR-samewords"]},{"n":5,"kind":"match","prompt":"At certain times of year, guests must stay for at least a week.","correct":5,"evidence":"can only be booked for a minimum of seven nights","why":{"en":"F: \"In July and August... a minimum of seven nights\" = at least a week at certain times.","tr":"F: \"Temmuz ve ağustosta... en az yedi gece\" = yılın belli zamanlarında en az bir hafta.","fa":"F: «در ژوئیه و اوت... حداقل هفت شب» یعنی در زمان‌های خاصی دست‌کم یک هفته."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]}]},{"text":1,"instruction":"Questions 6-14. Do the following statements agree with the information given in the text? In boxes 6-14 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","qtype":"tfng","questions":[{"n":6,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"In the old town, vehicles must give way to people on foot.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"pedestrians always have right of way","why":{"en":"\"Pedestrians always have right of way\": vehicles must give way.","tr":"\"Yayaların her zaman geçiş üstünlüğü var\": araçlar yol vermeli.","fa":"«عابرها همیشه حق تقدم دارند»: ماشین‌ها باید راه بدهند."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":7,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Cyclists are not permitted on the riverside path.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"it is shared with cyclists","why":{"en":"The path \"is shared with cyclists\", so they are allowed.","tr":"Yol \"bisikletlilerle ortak kullanılıyor\", yani onlara izin var.","fa":"مسیر «با دوچرخه‌سوارها مشترک است»، پس مجازند."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":8,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Places on the free walking tours must be reserved in advance.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"There is no need to book","why":{"en":"\"There is no need to book: simply turn up.\"","tr":"\"Rezervasyona gerek yok: sadece gelin.\"","fa":"«لازم نیست رزرو کنی: فقط بیا»."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":9,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"The walking tours are offered in several languages.","correct":"NOT GIVEN","evidence":"The guides are local volunteers","why":{"en":"The text gives the guides, the times and the length, but no languages.","tr":"Metin rehberleri, saatleri ve süreyi veriyor ama dillerden söz etmiyor.","fa":"متن راهنماها، ساعت‌ها و مدت را می‌گوید، اما از زبان‌ها حرفی نمی‌زند."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":10,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Visitors can get a printed map at the main railway station.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"Free paper maps are available from the information desk at the central railway station","why":{"en":"\"Free paper maps... at the central railway station\": printed = paper; main = central.","tr":"\"Ücretsiz kâğıt haritalar... merkez tren istasyonunda\": printed = paper; main = central.","fa":"«نقشه‌های کاغذی رایگان... در ایستگاه مرکزی قطار»: printed یعنی paper و main یعنی central."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":11,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"The city app shows where the public toilets are.","correct":"NOT GIVEN","evidence":"shows step-free routes for people with pushchairs or wheelchairs","why":{"en":"The app shows step-free routes and pharmacies. Toilets are not mentioned.","tr":"Uygulama basamaksız yolları ve eczaneleri gösteriyor. Tuvaletlerden söz edilmiyor.","fa":"اپ مسیرهای بدون پله و داروخانه‌ها را نشان می‌دهد. از توالت حرفی نیست."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":12,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"All the street lamps in the centre stay on throughout the night.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"every second street lamp is switched off to save energy","why":{"en":"After 1 am \"every second street lamp is switched off\".","tr":"Gece 1’den sonra \"her iki sokak lambasından biri kapatılıyor\".","fa":"بعد از ساعت ۱ بامداد «یکی در میان چراغ‌های خیابان خاموش می‌شود»."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":13,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Victoria Park can be used after dark.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"Victoria Park remains open all night","why":{"en":"\"Victoria Park remains open all night.\" Keeping to the lit avenue is only a preference.","tr":"\"Victoria Park bütün gece açık kalıyor.\" Aydınlık caddeyi kullanmak yalnızca bir tercih.","fa":"«پارک ویکتوریا تمام شب باز است». ماندن در خیابان اصلیِ روشن فقط یک ترجیح است."},"trap":["TR-hedge"]},{"n":14,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"It is against the law to wear headphones while crossing a road.","correct":"NOT GIVEN","evidence":"We recommend that walkers do not wear headphones","why":{"en":"\"We recommend\" is advice. The text says nothing about the law.","tr":"\"Öneriyoruz\" bir tavsiyedir. Metin kanun hakkında bir şey söylemiyor.","fa":"«توصیه می‌کنیم» یک توصیه است. متن درباره‌ی قانون چیزی نمی‌گوید."},"trap":["TR-hedge","TR-NGvsF"]}]}],"id":"c-x05-r1-d-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-05","unit":"x05-r1"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"paraphrase","point":1,"prompt":"A question says \"suitable for wheelchair users\". Which words in a review would match?","options":["a lift to the roof garden is planned","close to the bus stop","step-free access throughout"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"Step-free access means no steps, so a wheelchair can get in.","tr":"Basamaksız giriş, basamak yok demek; tekerlekli sandalye girebilir.","fa":"ورودی بدون پله یعنی پله ندارد، پس ویلچر می‌تواند وارد شود."}},{"tests":"word","point":3,"prompt":"A notice says walkers \"have right of way\". This means they...","options":["must walk on the right","can go first, and drivers must wait","need a permit"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"Right of way = the right to go first.","tr":"Right of way = önce geçme hakkı.","fa":"right of way یعنی حق اول رد شدن."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"Questions 1-5 have six reviews, A-F. What do you know about the letters?","options":["A letter can be used twice, and some may not be used","Each letter is used exactly once","You must use all six letters"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"\"NB You may use any letter more than once\": with five questions and six letters, some letters are left over.","tr":"\"NB Herhangi bir harfi birden fazla kullanabilirsin\": beş soru ve altı harf olunca bazı harfler artar.","fa":"«NB می‌توانی هر حرفی را بیش از یک بار به کار ببری»: با پنج سؤال و شش حرف، بعضی حرف‌ها اضافه می‌مانند."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Text: \"We advise visitors to wear a helmet.\" Statement: \"Visitors must wear a helmet by law.\"","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"Advice is given; nothing is said about the law.","tr":"Bir tavsiye veriliyor; kanun hakkında bir şey söylenmiyor.","fa":"یک توصیه داده شده؛ درباره‌ی قانون چیزی گفته نشده."}}],"id":"c-x05-r1-x-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-05","unit":"x05-r1"}}}; })(globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS = globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS || {});
